  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Small Arms &amp; Light Weapons in Jamaica - (SALIENT JAMAICA) Joi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Reducing Small Arms &amp; Light Weapons in Jamaica joint programme is geared at reducing violence and the proliferation of illicit firearms. The joint programme is aligned to Jamaica&apos;s National Development Goal 2- &quot;The Jamaican society is secure, cohesive and just&quot; and several Sustainable Development Goals, and will be jointly implemented by the following UN entities: UNDP, UNODA, UNLIREC, UNODC, UNESCO.

UNESCO, as lead UN agency on Quality Education, will address conflict resolution in a school setting strengthening educator&apos;s capacities as well as by enhancing youth empowerment, strengthening capacities of youth for them to become responsible citizens.</narrative>
  </description>
